WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.979 --> 00:00:05.310
Finding Dory floats onto the big screen this
summer and sees the return of Pixar's plucky

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.870
clownfish Nemo and our favourite funny and
forgetful blue tang Dory.

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:13.919
In this sequel to Finding Nemo, Dory's memory
is triggered by a stingray migration and she

00:00:13.919 --> 00:00:17.630
sets off on a quest to find her family with
the help of Marlin and Nemo.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:22.099
Finding Dory promises to explore a new chapter
in Nemo's ocean world, so let's take a look

00:00:22.099 --> 00:00:25.369
at the new and returning characters we can
look forward to meeting in the movie.

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:30.490
First up is Destiny, a whale shark, voiced
by Kaitlin Olson, star of It's Always Sunny

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:31.519
In Philadelphia.

00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:36.329
Destiny has difficulty swimming straight due
to poor eyesight, and realising there's something

00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:41.289
familiar about Dory, she befriends the blue
tang when she visits the Marine Life Institute.

00:00:41.289 --> 00:00:46.120
Whale sharks are the largest fish in the sea
and Destiny herself is not only very big-hearted

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.370
but also speaks whale.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:52.359
Which is very handy, because at the Marine
Life Institute, Destiny is friendly with Bailey,

00:00:52.359 --> 00:00:56.910
a beluga whale, although they do like to poke
fun at each other, with Bailey calling Destiny

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:01.629
a whale, rather than a shark, and Destiny
making fun of Bailey's huge head.

00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:05.610
Bailey thinks his biological sonar skills
don't work properly, although the Institute's

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.590
doctors don't seem to think there's anything
really wrong with him.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.520
Bailey is voiced by Modern Family star Ty
Burrell.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.070
Speaking of Modern Family, Ed O'Neill, Ty
Burell's co-star from the hit comedy series,

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:21.890
voices Hank the octopus, who is strictly just
a septopus, as he's only got seven tentacles.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:26.580
Hank is adept at camouflage and escaping from
tricky situations, and he's the first to greet

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.861
Dory at the Marine Life Institute, but he's
only willing to help her in return for "a

00:01:30.861 --> 00:01:35.750
ticket on a transport truck to a cozy Cleveland
facility where he'll be able to enjoy a peaceful

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:37.450
life of solitude."

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:41.970
In Finding Dory, Marlin and Nemo come across
a pair of snoozing sea lions called Fluke

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.780
and Rudder just outside the Marine Life Institute.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:48.890
They're voiced by British actors Idris Elba
and Dominic West who worked together on the

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:51.640
critically acclaimed crime drama series The
Wire.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:56.310
Director Andrew Stanton has said he wanted
Fluke and Rudder to sound like British gangster-style

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:57.920
talking sea lions.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.310
When Nemo and Marlin encounter them, they're
resting on a sought-after rock and don't enjoy

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:06.520
having their nap disturbed, although their
"bark is far worse than their bite."

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.979
Dory's mother Jenny is voiced by Annie Hall
star Diane Keaton and her father Charlie is

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:13.409
played by American Pie's Eugene Levy.

00:02:13.409 --> 00:02:16.849
Dory's parents don't suffer from quite the
same memory loss as Dory.

00:02:16.849 --> 00:02:21.349
Jenny is upbeat and a little flighty, but
she loves Dory dearly and wants to be a good

00:02:21.349 --> 00:02:22.459
role model for her.

00:02:22.459 --> 00:02:26.480
Charlie likes to have fun, although his jokes
probably aren't as good as he'd like to think

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.480
they are.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.900
Still, the most important thing to them is
"teaching their memory-challenged daughter

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:31.900
how to survive."

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:37.090
Loons replace the seagulls from Finding Nemo,
and in Finding Dory we meet Becky, an offbeat,

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:41.489
kooky loon who takes a shine to Marlin, and
although Nemo is sceptical about her, she's

00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:44.860
probably cleverer than she looks.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:46.940
The returning cast include Dory, Nemo and
Marlin of course!

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:51.340
In Finding Dory, Nemo has gone back to school
after his big adventure in Finding Nemo, and

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:55.349
is the first to offer his help to Dory when
she decides to embark on her ocean search

00:02:55.349 --> 00:02:56.359
for her family.

00:02:56.359 --> 00:03:00.400
Nemo's father Marlin is more hesitant about
jumping in with Dory's mission to head to

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.810
the California coast, but he understands what
it's like to lose family, and Dory of course

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.510
helped him to find Nemo.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:11.080
The spotted-eagle-ray teacher, Mr Ray, will
be back, and this time Dory will be his perky

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:15.299
teacher's assistant during his student field
trips around the coral reef and seabed.

00:03:15.299 --> 00:03:20.140
The cool ocean turtles Crush and his son Squirt
return again happy to "lend a flipper to a

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.430
fish in need."

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:25.340
And the Tank Gang who escaped from the dentist's
office at the end of Finding Nemo will also

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:26.910
be back for the sequel.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:31.689
Expected to return are the Moorish Idol fish,
Gill, and Deb, the blue and white damselfish

00:03:31.689 --> 00:03:34.959
who believed her reflection in the fish tank
was her sister Flo.

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:38.739
And many fellow Pixar fans are hoping that
we'll see the French shrimp Jacques from the

00:03:38.739 --> 00:03:40.779
dentist's office make a comeback too.

00:03:40.779 --> 00:03:44.879
Sadly, the original voice actor Joe Ranft
died between the making of the two films,

00:03:44.879 --> 00:03:48.099
but it's hoped that his brother Jerome may
step in to the role.

00:03:48.099 --> 00:03:52.469
John Ratzenberger is rumoured to cameo again
in Finding Dory as the voice of the school

00:03:52.469 --> 00:03:54.620
of Moonfish who appeared in Finding Nemo.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:59.639
And finally, there will be sea otters in Finding
Dory, lots of cute, adorable otters!

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:02.959
So guys, who's your favourite character from
Finding Nemo?

00:04:02.959 --> 00:04:05.219
And how excited are you for the sequel?

00:04:05.219 --> 00:04:07.439
I'd love to hear your thoughts in the comments
below.

